All you need to do is model average the density estimates which can be
done with either the total estimate or the individual stratum estimates
that DISTANCE produces.  Unless you have small sample sizes like Rich or
poor data, much of this is a rather academic question because the
abundance estimates vary little between detection models which is why it
has never been much of a pressing issue. That could change in expanding
distance sampling to a full likelihood approach that models abundance
spatially as well as detection.

