Jeff, Len

Thanks very much. Indeed, your first paragraph summarizes what I'd done, and
what I found.

I re-did the bootstrap run, saving the file this time, and was able to take
the mean density point estimate across all thousand runs (and confirmed that
the models selected corresponded with their AICc rankings in an approximate
way). 95centiles from this output were also easily obtained. I'd gotten
bootstrap warnings, but no actual errors -- all the data appeared to be
there, as advertised. This seems to me a reasonable way to proceed.

I'm not sure I fully understand your alternative suggestion. I need to go
get B&A 2nd edition from the library (have only 1st edition on my shelf).
Won't this require having AICc model weights available? I haven't seen
anywhere in DISTANCE output that these are provided.

Best regards,

Rich Harris
